			"Message": "docs(Sky): Normalize emoji spacing and update version references in docs\n\nReplace literal emoji characters with HTML numeric entities (&#x2001;) in\nArchitecture.md and README.md to ensure consistent rendering across all\nmarkdown parsers and diff viewers. Update the Astro version badge from v5.x\nto match the current Astro 7.x dependency, and correct the estimated line\ncount for SkyBridge (~1,000 lines, down from ~2,900) and astro.config.ts\n(~2,000 lines, up from ~1,450) to reflect the current state of the codebase.\n\nCollapse the sponsor table cell formatting to single-line markdown for\nconsistency with other CodeEditorLand repo READMEs. Streamline the key\ndependencies table by removing terminal packages (@xterm/xterm, addon-\npackages, drag-drop, search-dev-extension, vscode-languagedetection,\ndotenv, deepmerge-ts, zod) and adding vite-plugin-top-level-await and\ntypescript v6.x, matching the actual package.json. Add Wind, Mountain,\nCocoon, and Worker emoji identifiers to the \"In the Land Project\" table\nfor visual consistency with the rest of the README.\n\nNo functional changes to Sky's runtime behavior.",
